          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For real random variables $(X_n)$ and $X$ on one probability space, write\n$X_n\\to X$ **in probability** when, for every $\\varepsilon>0$,\n$$\\mathbb P(|X_n-X|>\\varepsilon)\\longrightarrow0.$$\nThis is precisely [[def-convergence-in-measure]] for the probability measure.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
